    "mode": "gate",
    "physical_scope": "59 exact Metal tests: native aggregate reduction, tight and formula oracles, their overlapping checks matching synchronous ones, ordinary formula CLI paths with partial coverage and writer errors, complete-world-view collection, bounded relation equality filtering with 8/16/32-bit column transport, shared-context composition with compute-pass timestamps attributed to their own batches, contention and shared failure handling, a stop during an overlapping check's production observing its submission and a panic there invalidating the context, caller-supplied session resources with policy and observer failures, observed complete collection on supplied contexts, explicit formula profiles with independent oracle state, compilation identity and each fitted workgroup size compiled once at its first dispatch (a refused compilation failing its check), fixed sizes compiled with their kernel, primitives selecting over a prefetched adapter enumeration as their independent constructors do, and combined language-consumer families with scored observations and optimum ties. Cooperative device control, interrupted preparation reuse and actual submission receipts are included, alongside completed-support table joins with actual GPU candidates and complete CPU/Metal answer families, and the quantified series' families through the batched completion with each residual root's inner preparation. Ordinary automatic membership sessions check complete tight families, the general device route for non-tight theories, and tight work refusal before dispatch. An ordinary session grows its adaptive candidate slates during steady enumeration, and an enumeration proposes its next slate while the device checks the current one, on each device route, with the CPU family. Terminal sessions check complete reconstruction from device-verified base answers. Hybrid device sessions check original acceptance, objective ties, constraint failures, queued cancellation and reconstruction after streamed host constraints. Unlisted tests and Vulkan are not selected.",
